{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/915168-newbie-needing-some-help","id":915168,"title":"Newbie needing some help","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-15T16:18:27-07:00","id":915168,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon10.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Newbie needing some help","content":"So i picked up a copy of Vampire Requiem at 2nd and Charles and wanted to introduce my rp group to it. There were somethings either i missed in the book or just can't find. <br /> First is merits I know at character creation you pick 10 but after that can you gain merits by using exp like it would take 2 exp for a two dot merit<br /> <br /> Bloodlines i have a book and three more coming. i know you have to be in a parent clan to join line but past that is there anything else i need to know.<br /> <br /> thanks in advance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11973-nightshroud","name":"NightShroud","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T16:21:28-07:00","id":915172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NightShroud</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/915168-newbie-needing-some-help#post915168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">merits I know at character creation you pick 10 but after that can you gain merits by using exp like it would take 2 exp for a two dot merit</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. Page 83, at the bottom of the Vampire Creation Quick Reference, has the experience costs for buying traits up, and Merit dots are listed. You guessed it right, a Merit costs one experience per dot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T16:49:00-07:00","id":915184,"title":"","content":"Thank you. i prefer this game to dnd though most of our group hasn't played anything else and i remember playing Masquerade. I love the update to Requiem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11973-nightshroud","name":"NightShroud","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T11:49:44-07:00","id":915742,"title":"","content":"Another question about bloodlines. If you create a charcter and they join a bloodline do the disiplines replace the claan diciplines or do you get to pick rhose disciplines at chacter creation. Thanks again","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11973-nightshroud","name":"NightShroud","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T11:58:26-07:00","id":915747,"title":"","content":"That's ST's perogative. If they say the new discipline spread is available at character creation as in clan, then yes. As an occasional ST myself, I don't allow those 'embraced straight into the bloodline' characters to buy bloodline gained disciplines to be purchased with the starting discipline allocation points, but I do allow them to be purchased at in clan prices with starting XP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T12:04:52-07:00","id":915750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/915168-newbie-needing-some-help?p=915747#post915747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's ST's perogative. If they say the new discipline spread is available at character creation as in clan, then yes. As an occasional ST myself, I don't allow those 'embraced straight into the bloodline' characters to buy bloodline gained disciplines to be purchased with the starting discipline allocation points, but I do allow them to be purchased at in clan prices with starting XP.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes sense. Im new to storytelling and i want to be able to answer questions my friends have. I do appriate the help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11973-nightshroud","name":"NightShroud","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T13:30:54-07:00","id":915807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NightShroud</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/915168-newbie-needing-some-help?p=915742#post915742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another question about bloodlines. If you create a charcter and they join a bloodline do the disiplines replace the claan diciplines or do you get to pick rhose disciplines at chacter creation. Thanks again</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If your character's sire was in that bloodline you can opt to be in that bloodline so RAW you can choose that discipline spread. Some story tellers ( as Tsusasi said) do not allow this, but it is rules as written and not allowing it would be a house rule. If you are in a bloodline, then those disciplines <b>replace </b>the clan ones. <br /> <br /> They are clan price because that is your list. There is no more clan list because it was replaced by your bloodline list. I hope that makes sense. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T13:46:30-07:00","id":915821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/915168-newbie-needing-some-help?p=915807#post915807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If your character's sire was in that bloodline you can opt to be in that bloodline so RAW you can choose that discipline spread. Some story tellers ( as Tsusasi said) do not allow this, but it is rules as written and not allowing it would be a house rule. If you are in a bloodline, then those disciplines <b>replace </b>the clan ones.<br /> <br /> They are clan price because that is your list. There is no more clan list because it was replaced by your bloodline list. I hope that makes sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very much so thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11973-nightshroud","name":"NightShroud","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}